  "term": "pull model",
  "definition": "The pull model refers to the part of a push-pull framework that explains behavior in terms of attractive forces drawing a person toward a destination, option, or alternative. In this broader model, behavior is understood as the outcome of opposing forces of attraction and repulsion.",
